 Road for wooded trails and scenic viewpoints; bring the official park map and use only designated picnic sites.","short_summary":"A large natural park offering marked hiking terrain, viewpoints, and designated picnic areas.","evidence_claim":"Prospect Hill Park at 314 Totten Pond Road covers 273.07 acres and contains wooded hiking trails, scenic vistas, and designated picnic sites.","source_url":"https://www.city.waltham.ma.us/1939/Prospect-Hill-Park","source_title":"Prospect Hill Park | Waltham, MA","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The seasonal vehicle-access road opens daily at 10:00 a.m.; consult the city page and park map for current access rules.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"stonehurst-robert-treat-paine-drive","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Stonehurst, The Robert Treat Paine Estate","title":"Walk a Historic Estate Landscape","subtitle":"Robert Treat Paine Drive corridor — landmark grounds","notes":"Call before heading to 100 Robert Treat Paine Drive, since private rentals close the immediate grounds and guided tours require appointments.","short_summary":"A National Historic Landmark estate with year-round landscape access when private events permit.","evidence_claim":"Stonehurst is a historic landmark at 100 Robert Treat Paine Drive; its grounds open year-round from sunrise to sunset, while guided tours are appointment-only.","source_url":"https://www.city.waltham.ma.us/1755/Stonehurst-The-Robert-Treat-Paine-Estate","source_title":"Stonehurst, The Robert Treat Paine Estate | Waltham, MA","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Grounds normally open sunrise to sunset, but the estate closes during private rentals. Call ahead; guided tours require an appointment.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"lyman-estate-lyman-street","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Lyman Estate","title":"Tour a Federal-Era Estate","subtitle":"Lyman Street corridor — mansion, gardens, and greenhouses","notes":"Plan a first- or third-Saturday visit to 185 Lyman Street, or walk the grounds during public hours; check for private-event closures first.","short_summary":"A National Historic Landmark pairing a Federal-style mansion with gardens and historic greenhouses.","evidence_claim":"The Lyman Estate at 185 Lyman Street is a 1793 National Historic Landmark with a mansion, preserved gardens, historic greenhouses, and 37 acres.","source_url":"https://www.historicnewengland.org/property/lyman-estate/","source_title":"Lyman Estate | Historic New England","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"House tours are offered on the first and third Saturdays; grounds are generally open dawn to dusk but close during private rentals.","cost_status":"purchase_required","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"gore-place-gore-street","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Gore Place","title":"Explore a Museum and Working Farm","subtitle":"Gore Street corridor — mansion, farm, and open grounds","notes":"Use 52 Gore Street for the entrance, explore the grounds between dawn and dusk, and check the calendar before adding a mansion tour or program.","short_summary":"A nineteenth-century estate combining a museum, working farm, and extensive public green space.","evidence_claim":"Gore Place at 52 Gore Street includes a nineteenth-century mansion museum, 50 acres of green space, and a working farm; its grounds are free to visit.","source_url":"https://goreplace.org/visit","source_title":"Visit - Gore Place","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Grounds are free and open dawn to dusk daily unless a special event is underway. Mansion tours and some programs require paid tickets.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"mass-central-rail-trail-beaver-street","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Mass Central Rail Trail — Waltham Segment","title":"Take the Shared-Use Trail West","subtitle":"Beaver Street corridor — Waltham rail-trail access","notes":"Join the named Waltham segment near Beaver Street for an off-road walk or ride, and consult the state status page before attempting longer connections.","short_summary":"A three-mile Waltham shared-use segment within the developing regional trail network.","evidence_claim":"The state reports that Waltham completed a three-mile Mass Central Rail Trail segment from Beaver Street to Route 117/Hillside Road in 2023.","source_url":"https://www.mass.gov/info-details/mass-central-rail-trail-wayside","source_title":"Mass Central Rail Trail - Wayside","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Review the state project-status page before traveling because connecting segments remain in different stages of completion.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
